<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Douglas MacArthur</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1880–1964</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Douglas MacArthur was an American general who served as military adviser to the Commonwealth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a> from 1935 and commanded Allied forces in the South-West Pacific during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>. As <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/supreme-commander-for-the-allied-powers">Supreme Commander for the Allied Powers</a> he directed the occupation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> from 1945 to 1951, overseeing disarmament and a new democratic constitution. He was dismissed during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korean-war">Korean War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/douglas-macarthur.jpg" alt="Douglas MacArthur" width="320" height="405" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Photographer not credited. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MacArthur_Manila_(cropped2)(b).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
